# Multi-Omics Integration of Copy-Number Alterations, Somatic Mutations, and Pathway-Level Transcriptomics Improves Prognostic Stratification and Clinical Decision Utility Across 3,186 Breast Cancer Patients

**Muhammad Nadeem**  
Department of Bioinformatics and Biotechnology, Government College University Faisalabad, Faisalabad, Pakistan  
*Correspondence:* muhmmad.nadeem.bioinfo@gmail.com  

---

## Abstract

**Background:** Breast cancer progression is governed by coordinated somatic copy-number alterations (CNAs), driver point mutations, and transcriptional pathway dysregulation, yet most prognostic models rely on single-omics gene panels or anatomical staging alone.  
**Methods:** We developed and externally validated a strictly leakage-free, platform-invariant three-layer multi-omics survival framework integrating GISTIC2 focal CNAs, somatic non-silent mutations, tumor mutational burden (TMB), curated protein-coding mRNA expression, and single-sample Gene Set Enrichment Analysis (ssGSEA) MSigDB Hallmark pathway activity scores across $N = 3,186$ primary breast cancer patients: TCGA-BRCA ($n = 994$; 5-fold stratified out-of-fold cross-validation plus a locked 80/20 discovery [$n = 795$] and internal holdout [$n = 199$] split), METABRIC ($n = 1,865$), and GEO GSE20685 ($n = 327$). Elastic-Net Cox proportional hazards (`CoxNet`), Random Survival Forest (`RSF`), and Gradient Boosted Survival Analysis (`GBSA`) were benchmarked against clinical covariates (`Age + Stage/NPI`) and re-trained commercial gene panels (`Oncotype DX` and `PAM50`) using 1,000-bootstrap Harrell’s concordance index (C-index), time-dependent 1-, 3-, and 5-year dynamic ROC-AUC, and 5-year Decision Curve Analysis (DCA).  
**Results:** Elastic-Net Cox regularization selected a parsimonious 42-feature three-omics signature integrating 4 focal CNA drivers (`ERBB2`, `CDK4`, `CDK6`, `PIK3CA`), 4 somatic mutations (`TP53`, `PIK3CA`, `KMT2C`, `AKT1`), 7 Hallmark pathways (`ESTROGEN_RESPONSE_LATE`, `P53_PATHWAY`, `ADIPOGENESIS`, `BILE_ACID_METABOLISM`, `COAGULATION`, `MYOGENESIS`, `SPERMATOGENESIS`), and 27 protein-coding transcripts. Across full TCGA-BRCA 5-fold out-of-fold evaluation ($n = 994$), `Clinico-3Omics` fusion achieved a C-index of $0.7185$ (95% CI: $0.6676\text{--}0.7715$) and a mean 1–5 year dynamic AUC of $0.7260$. In zero-shot external validation on METABRIC ($n = 1,865$), `Clinico-3Omics` ($\text{C-index} = 0.6202$, 95% CI: $0.6041\text{--}0.6374$; $\text{Mean AUC} = 0.6161$) outperformed `Oncotype DX` ($\text{C-index} = 0.5733$, $\text{AUC} = 0.5550$) and `PAM50` ($\text{C-index} = 0.5173$, $\text{AUC} = 0.5067$) panels, while the transcriptomic signature generalized to GSE20685 ($n = 327$, $\text{C-index} = 0.6642$, $\text{AUC} = 0.7005$). Applying the locked TCGA-Train median cutoff ($-0.0077$) without threshold re-tuning stratified METABRIC overall survival at log-rank $p = 3.06 \times 10^{-19}$, maintaining independent prognostic significance in multivariable Cox regression ($\text{HR} = 1.151$ per SD, $p = 7.48 \times 10^{-6}$) and within both ER+/HER2- luminal ($n = 1,159$, $\text{HR} = 1.342$, $p = 4.47 \times 10^{-13}$) and triple-negative ($n = 299$, $\text{HR} = 1.308$, $p = 7.35 \times 10^{-4}$) subtypes. Five-year DCA confirmed superior net clinical benefit over clinical staging alone across threshold probabilities from 12% to 38%.  
**Conclusions:** Integrating focal copy-number drivers, somatic mutations, and pathway-level transcriptomics yields cross-platform prognostic discrimination superior to single-omics assays and identifies endocrine-resistant, immune-cold, and cell-cycle-activated breast tumors with actionable therapeutic vulnerabilities.

