## 3. Results

### 3.1 Three-Omics Signature Selection and Head-to-Head Benchmark Against Commercial Panels
Elastic-Net Cox modeling on the integrated three-omics matrix selected a **42-feature signature** spanning all three molecular layers: **4 focal copy-number drivers** (`CNA_ERBB2`, `CNA_CDK4`, `CNA_CDK6`, `CNA_PIK3CA`), **4 somatic mutations** (`SNV_TP53`, `SNV_PIK3CA`, `SNV_KMT2C`, `SNV_AKT1`), **7 MSigDB Hallmark pathways** (`ESTROGEN_RESPONSE_LATE`, `P53_PATHWAY`, `ADIPOGENESIS`, `BILE_ACID_METABOLISM`, `COAGULATION`, `MYOGENESIS`, `SPERMATOGENESIS`), and **27 protein-coding genes** (`EDA2R`, `STXBP5`, `CEBPD`, `DLK2`, `APOA5`, `POU3F2`, `FAM179A`, `FFAR2`, `CPT1A`, `MRAP2`, `NOS1`, `SMR3A`, `GRIK2`, `SERPINA1`, `TFPI2`, `FAM9C`, `GRIA3`, `GSTM4`, `MAFF`, `PXDNL`, `CAMK4`, `LIPH`, `FABP7`, `AKNAD1`, `SLC5A12`, `ZNF536`, `JPH3`).

In head-to-head external evaluation (**Table 1**, **Figure 1**), the 3-Omics Molecular Signature ($\text{C-index} = 0.5824$, 95% CI: $0.5656\text{--}0.5994$; $\text{Mean AUC} = 0.5930$) outperformed both re-trained `Oncotype DX` ($\text{C-index} = 0.5733$, $\text{AUC} = 0.5550$) and `PAM50` ($\text{C-index} = 0.5173$, $\text{AUC} = 0.5067$) panels in METABRIC ($n = 1,865$). Fusing the 3-Omics risk score with clinical covariates (`Clinico-3Omics-Fusion`) achieved a 5-fold out-of-fold C-index of **$0.7185$** (95% CI: $0.6676\text{--}0.7715$, $\text{Mean AUC} = 0.7260$) across full TCGA-BRCA ($n = 994$) and **$0.6202$** (95% CI: $0.6041\text{--}0.6374$, $\text{Mean AUC} = 0.6161$ vs. $0.5716$ for `Clinical-Only`) in METABRIC. In the transcriptomic-only external cohort `GSE20685` ($n = 327$), the transcriptomic signature achieved a C-index of **$0.6642$** ($\text{Mean AUC} = 0.7005$), surpassing `Oncotype DX` ($\text{C-index} = 0.5939$, $\text{AUC} = 0.6113$) and `PAM50` ($\text{C-index} = 0.6030$, $\text{AUC} = 0.6464$).

