### 3.3 SHAP Feature Attribution, Hallmark Vulnerabilities, and 5-Year Decision Curve Analysis
Permutation SHAP analysis (**Figure 4**) and Hallmark enrichment profiling (**Figure 5**) revealed that high-risk tumors are characterized by marked depletion of **Late Estrogen Response** ($\text{FDR} = 4.27 \times 10^{-44}$), **Interferon-$\gamma$ Response** ($\text{FDR} = 6.07 \times 10^{-6}$), and **Inflammatory Response** ($\text{FDR} = 1.44 \times 10^{-7}$), alongside hyperactivation of **E2F Cell-Cycle Targets** ($\text{FDR} = 1.90 \times 10^{-8}$) and selection of `CNA_CDK4`, `CNA_CDK6`, and `CNA_PIK3CA` copy-number alterations. Finally, 5-year Decision Curve Analysis across $1,808$ METABRIC patients (**Figure 6**) demonstrated that the `Clinico-3Omics` fusion model yields consistently higher net clinical benefit than clinical covariates alone (`Age + Stage`) across decision threshold probabilities from **12% to 38%**.

